      "id": "W7220676714",
      "doi": "10.1515/joc-2026-0402",
      "title": "Explainable SHAP-based feature selection for accurate and computationally efficient network response time prediction in optical communication networks",
      "authors": [
        "Shayma Wail Nourildean",
        "Thamer M. Jamel"
      ],
      "year": 2026,
      "venue": "Journal of Optical Communications",
      "venue_abbr": "J. Opt. Commun.",
      "rank_label": "未匹配 CIE 2023",
      "keywords": [
        "SHAP",
        "explainable machine learning",
        "feature selection",
        "optical networks",
        "network performance management",
        "model interpretability",
        "random forest",
        "gradient boosting",
        "XGBoost",
        "stacking ensemble",
        "computational efficiency"
      ],
      "url": "https://doi.org/10.1515/joc-2026-0402",
      "cited_by_count": 0,
      "importance": 1,
      "score_basis": {},
      "role": "root",
      "reading_url": "items/1f7a96d8-7538-4810-94c0-de7f09339133.html",
      "summary": "论文提出以SHAP解释模型并筛选关键网络参数的机器学习框架，在相同条件下比较多种回归模型及堆叠集成模型筛选前后的表现。摘要报告，特征筛选效果因模型而异：随机森林在筛选后获得最佳总体预测表现，MAE和RMSE分别改善3.90%和4.85%，训练时间减少12.79%；梯度提升的训练时间减少51.44%。研究还评估了RAM使用、推理延迟和模型大小。",
      "summary_basis": "本站解读 · abstract-only"
    },
